      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Exclusive: FCA pressures firms to do more to sort 760,000 accounts as watchdog urges families to use free tracking service</p><p>Child trust fund providers are being put under the spotlight to check they are treating savers fairly and doing all they can to reunite young people with lost accounts.</p><p>The Financial Conduct Authority (FCA) said about 760,000 accounts worth an average of £2,000 were yet to be claimed – more than £1.5bn in total – as it launched a review of the market.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/money/2026/sep/01/child-trust-fund-firms-face-review-over-efforts-to-find-who-owns-15bn-worth-of-pots\">Continue reading...</a>"
